+# Original FCC cross-filing notice and Airfone carrier filing locators
+
+Public derivative of the November 9, 2026 Eastern source review · TEL02–TEL04 / AUD016-A1 / TC05–TC06.
+
+Recovered **DA 98-1687**, released **August 21, 1998**, with its attached **July 31, 1998 PCIA letter and appendices**. The FCC historical server and the April 1, 2007 archive replay returned identical **211,005-byte** PDFs with SHA-256 `a9e3e825f7c6e98b9cf0582ee54d1a5156fabe2213d22956b3f2032a375a2425`. The notice directs electronic filers to submit to both **WT 98-20** and **WT 98-100**. These are now separate paths to the original comments. The agency's carrier docket locators below identify filings and leave their actual text open. [FCC historical PDF](https://transition.fcc.gov/Bureaus/Wireless/Public_Notices/1998/da981687.pdf) · [2007 archive replay](https://web.archive.org/web/20070401102006id_/http://www.fcc.gov:80/Bureaus/Wireless/Public_Notices/1998/da981687.pdf)
+
+## Parallel docket copies to test
+
+The original notice, physical p. 2 extracted lines 25–35, says comments on the PCIA letter would enter both proceedings, and gives a deadline of **15 days from Federal Register publication**. The published September 8 summary separately prints **September 23, 1998** (printed p. 47460, PDF p. 1 lines 23–24). The notice also describes paper-copy and diskette routes at PDF pp. 2–3, and distinguishes the diskette copy from the original. Attachment A begins at PDF p. 4. The July 31 cover identifies WT 98-20 at p. 5 lines 5–18. The associated letter begins p. 6 and its three appendix descriptions are at p. 8 lines 1–27. [Full notice, p. 2](https://transition.fcc.gov/Bureaus/Wireless/Public_Notices/1998/da981687.pdf#page=2) · [Federal Register notice](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-09-08/pdf/98-24005.pdf)
+
+| Indexed record | WT 98-100 | WT 98-20 |
+|---|---|---|
+| **DA 98-1687**, both received August 21, 1998, both **21 pages** | Submission **5000705077**, **6005544707.pdf**, disseminated `1998-11-27T18:12:42.000-05:00` | Submission **5000705081**, **6005544710.pdf**, disseminated `1998-11-27T18:14:51.000-05:00` |
+| **GTE**, both received September 23, 1998, both **7 pages** | Submission **215909**, **2159090001.pdf**, disseminated **September 27** | Submission **215952**, **2159520001.pdf**, disseminated **September 29** |
+| **AT&T Wireless**, both received September 23, 1998, both **3 pages** | Label **AT&T WIRELESS SERVICES**, submission **215850**, **2158500001.pdf**, disseminated **September 25** | Label **AT&T WIRELESS SERVICES IN**, submission **215873**, **2158730001.pdf**, disseminated **September 27** |
+
+Both notice records give the same authority number and count. The matching dates, types, page counts and dual-filing instruction make the September rows candidates for parallel filings. Separate document IDs, filer labels and dissemination dates remain as indexed. Obtain each body and compare cover, file stamps, text and attachments before identifying any pair as equivalent. The recovered historical copy is verified by its own content and two endpoints. The corresponding ECFS attachment bodies were not compared. [FCC WT 98-100 index](https://publicapi.fcc.gov/ecfs/filings?api_key=DEMO_KEY&proceedings.name=98-100&limit=100) · [FCC WT 98-20 index](https://publicapi.fcc.gov/ecfs/filings?api_key=DEMO_KEY&proceedings.name=98-20&limit=500)
+
+## Carrier submissions cited by the FCC
+
+- **GTE Service Corporation's August 3, 1998 comments.** WT 98-100 submission **212492**, **2124920001.pdf**, **17 pages**. The received date and party match FCC 03-203 p. 4 n. 31. Keep the distinct September 23 comments and the separate published request on the July 31 PCIA letter. [GTE attachment locator](https://www.fcc.gov/ecfs/document/212492/1) · [FCC 03-203, p. 4](https://docs.fcc.gov/public/attachments/FCC-03-203A1.pdf#page=4)
+- **AT&T Wireless Services, Inc.'s December 11, 2002 ex parte.** WT 98-100 submission **5508549681**, **6513397395.pdf**, **4 pages**, disseminated **December 13**. FCC 03-203 p. 4 n. 34 cites the filing by party and December 11 date. A separate ex parte was received **December 5** and disseminated **December 9**, submission **5508544845**, **6513392484.pdf**, **1 page**. The earlier document's relationship to the cited one remains open. [December 11 locator](https://www.fcc.gov/ecfs/document/5508549681/1) · [December 5 locator](https://www.fcc.gov/ecfs/document/5508544845/1)
+- **AT&T's July 12, 1994 reply.** GN 94-33 submission **132331**, **1323310001.pdf**, **25 pages**, labeled **REPLY TO COMMENTS**. This is a candidate for the AT&T reply cited at pp. 12–13 in FCC 98-134 p. 42 n. 255. The index alone leaves the content match open. The exact MSD-92-14 query returned zero rows and does not cover other record series or any unindexed filings. [GN 94-33 index](https://publicapi.fcc.gov/ecfs/filings?api_key=DEMO_KEY&proceedings.name=94-33&limit=100) · [FCC 98-134 p. 42](https://docs.fcc.gov/public/attachments/FCC-98-134A1.pdf#page=42)
+
+## File structure and access observations
+
+- **4 and 21 pages.** On both identical bodies, `file` reports **4 pages**. PyMuPDF, pypdf and Poppler report **21 pages** for the full body. The first byte prefix ending just after `%%EOF` at **13,584 bytes** gives four pages in PyMuPDF and pypdf. The final trailer references `/Prev 12900`. The two observed `startxref` values are **12900** and **208384**. Extracted text on the first four pages matches across the prefix and full body. The later pages supply the cover, letter and appendices. These structural checks leave the history of the source editions and either indexed ECFS attachment's bytes open. [FCC historical body](https://transition.fcc.gov/Bureaus/Wireless/Public_Notices/1998/da981687.pdf)
+- **Access.** The exact current links and tested API attachment URLs returned **HTTP 403 HTML** for the carrier items. Six Wayback availability results for the August GTE and December 11 AT&T filing URLs returned empty snapshot maps. The two guessed DA 98-1687 attachment links returned **HTTP 200 HTML** with page-not-found text. The historical FCC URL and its separate archive capture returned the notice PDF. Preserve the access observations by endpoint. A denied URL or empty availability result leaves retention and content open.
+- **Index counts.** The bounded queries returned **53** WT 98-100 rows, **218** WT 98-20 rows, **59** GN 94-33 rows, **8** CC 91-35 rows, **0** exact MSD-92-14 rows and **5** positive-control WT 12-155 rows. The initial date-filter query returned HTTP **400**. The subsequent WT 98-20 query used the docket alone. These are returned counts within the named tests.
+
+## Open inputs
+
+Obtain the August 3 GTE filing, both December AT&T ex partes, both versions of the September 23 comments, and the original MSD-92-14 petition and attachments. Compare the carrier statements on service-specific operator assistance and billing with the rules in force and the original September 2001 switch, operator and billing records. The field dictionary and event IDs remain necessary to test the disputed call entries. The recovered notice and PCIA material concern the filing process and proposals. No disputed call was assigned to a service or carrier leg.
+
+The FAA corrected answer and receipt, signed action or no-action determination, recommendation dispositions and applicable case routing remain deferred. This telephone acquisition leaves the five-track work plan open.
+
+Reading covered the notice, the attached July 31 cover and letter, the appendix introduction and appendix title or end-page controls, the cited Federal Register text, and selected FCC index fields. The underlying carrier filing bodies were inaccessible on the tested routes. Only original analysis and public source locators are included in the publication payload.
